# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Structure:
#   /                   encrypted landing (js-auth)
#   /product.html       product page (encrypted)
#   /docs/              docs tree (encrypted, multi-page)
#   /brand.html         brand book (encrypted)
#   /playground.html    email-gate page (encrypted)
#   /playground/        the dashboards app (NOT encrypted — gated by email)

# Friendly short paths.
#
# Targets are the URL Cloudflare actually serves (extensionless for files,
# trailing slash for directories). Pointing an alias at /playground.html made
# it a 302 into Pages' own 308 -> /playground, i.e. two hops for one click.
#
# /demo is NOT an alias any more: landing/demo/index.html is a real 75 KB page
# and this rule was shadowing it, so /demo was unreachable at its own URL.
# The dashboards gate keeps /gate and /dashboards.
/gate         /playground         301
/dashboards   /playground         301
/app          /playground/        301
/bench        /benchmarks/        301
/github       https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj 302

# The Jev write-up moved to the blog (2026-09-21). One canonical page — the
# numbers must never live in two places. Named source only, never a catch-all;
# #fragment requests keep their fragment through the 301. Deliberately NO
# `.html` sibling rule: seo_lint rule 64 hard-gates any published `.html`
# spelling (the site's URL contract is extensionless, and a `.html` source
# here would be dead bytes after Pages' own 308) — legacy `.html` deep links
# to the removed file get the real 404 page, which is the honest answer.
/benchmarks/decisions  /blog/does-xerj-beat-jev  301

# Installer fallback (#740). /get.sh is normally answered by functions/get.js
# (it's in _routes.json), which counts the request and serves the installer.
# This 200-rewrite only fires if Functions are disabled, so /get.sh serves the
# real installer body (same file as /get) instead of falling to the SPA/404 and
# piping HTML to sh. No drift: it points at /get, not a copy. Not a catch-all.
/get.sh       /get                200

# Trailing slash normalization
/home         /                   301

# Google Search Console 404s (read 2026-10-25). Each source below is a URL
# Googlebot actually requested; each target is the page that answers it.
# Named sources only, never a pattern.
#
# Guessed agent-file paths. There is no static install.md or SKILL.md on this
# site: `xerj init` writes the skill files into the user's project, so an
# agent that guesses them is sent to the install page and the agent index.
/docs/install.md    /docs/install       301
/SKILL.md           /llms.txt           301
